  "id": "Compound::DB06414 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Etravirine is a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI) that is included in the class of non-nucleoside analogs, which includes Nevirapine. Both Etravirine and Nevirapine bind to Cyp3a4, a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of many drugs. This binding is supported by multiple paths in the dataset, with the lowest common ancestor of Etravirine and Nevirapine being classified as a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor and an organonitrogen heterocyclic compound. The shared mechanism of binding to Cyp3a4 suggests a potential pharmacological interaction between these compounds and the enzyme. The evidence is consistent across different paths, with the lowest common ancestor linking the two entities to the same biological pathway. The mechanism of action is primarily through direct binding to Cyp3a4, which may lead to altered drug metabolism and potentially increased toxicity. The integration of these paths supports a plausible mechanism of action, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the clinical relevance.",
